    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L01-ACTIVITY-015",
      "SourceSection": "1.3: Where is the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Consider the height of the end of a second hand on a clock over a full minute. It starts pointing up, then rotates to point down, then rotates until it is pointing straight up again. This motion repeats once every minute.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l01.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L01-ACTIVITY-016",
      "SourceSection": "1.3: Where is the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "If we imagine the clock centered at \\((0,0)\\) on the coordinate plane, then we can study the movement of the end of the second hand by thinking about its \\((x,y)\\) coordinates on the plane. Over one minute, the \\(y\\)-coordinate starts at…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l01.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L01-ACTIVITY-017",
      "SourceSection": "1.3: Where is the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "While we have worked with many types of functions, such as rational or exponential, none of them are characterized by output values that repeat over and over again, so we can’t use them to model the height of the end of the second hand.…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l01.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L01-ACTIVITY-018",
      "SourceSection": "1.3: Where is the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The length of an interval at which a periodic function repeats. A function \\(f\\) has a period, \\(p\\), if \\(f(x+p) = f(x)\\) for all inputs \\(x\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l01.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L01-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "1.3: Where is the Point?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A function whose values repeat at regular intervals. If \\(f\\) is a periodic function then there is a number \\(p\\), called the period, so that \\(f(x + p) = f(x)\\) for all inputs \\(x\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u06-l01.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
